FILE = HEAD .

HEAD =
  "# js: the JavaScript proofs"
  "Candidates **for consideration**, outside the locked `coq/` registry (AGENTS.md:"
  "no new Coq proof files). In `PROOF_CANONIZATION.md`'s levels every check here is"
  "**P1**: a finite, computable check, and a target for a P0 Coq proof later. Nothing"
  "here enters the deterministic core on its own."
  "| Folder | What it holds |"
  "|--------|---------------|"
  "| `catalog/` | the I-series checks, one module per record (`I-122.ts` is the roll-up of I-108 … I-151) |"
  "| `spo/` | the subject-predicate-object index of numeric constants: `triples.mjs` (golden and must-reject), `predicates.mjs`, `check.mjs`, `index.json` |"
  "| `vm/` | every record's check as one classic script, in two base64 dialects: `<TAG>.b64` and `<TAG>.b64url` |"
  "| `tools/` | `build.mjs` (catalogue and documents), `vm.mjs` (tags, scripts, dialects, the vm and Worker runs) |"
  "| `catalog.json` | every record: tag, title, category, owner, statements, carriers, whether it holds |"
  "The documents are in `../js-docs/`, one RFC-style page per record and the registry"
  "`JS-PROOF-INDEX.md`. They are built from the checks, so they say only what the"
  "checks check."
  "## Tags"
  "Each record's tag is its number in base 36 and its letter, uppercase, in `/A-Z0-9/`:"
  "I-108 is `30`, I-141 is `3X`, I-127b is `3JB`. The tag decodes back to the record."
  "## Carriers"
  "Each check, with its TypeScript types stripped and its imports replaced by names"
  "the host supplies (`assert`; `os` and `process` where used), is one classic script"
  "that `vm.Script` compiles and a Worker runs as it is. It is stored twice, as"
  "standard base64 and as URL-safe base64; both decode to the same bytes. The build"
  "runs every record both ways and records the result: a check that holds on a main"
  "thread but not in a Worker says so in its document."
  "## Run"
  "```"
  "make js          # the SPO index, then every catalogue check"
  "make js-docs     # rebuild catalog.json, vm/ and ../js-docs/ from the checks"
  "```"
  .
